    "abstract": "SAM simultaneously minimises loss value and loss sharpness by seeking parameters whose neighbourhoods have uniformly low loss. The min-max problem admits an efficient first-order approximation requiring one extra forward/backward pass. SAM improves generalization across CIFAR-10/100, ImageNet and fine-tuning tasks, provides robustness to label noise, and the paper introduces m-sharpness.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "Minimising max_{||eps||<=rho} L(w + eps) improves generalization, motivated by a PAC-Bayesian bound.",
      "The inner maximisation is approximated by eps_hat = rho g / ||g||, costing one extra gradient computation per step.",
      "SAM improves test error over SGD across architectures on CIFAR-10, CIFAR-100, and ImageNet, and in fine-tuning.",
      "SAM provides robustness to label noise comparable to dedicated noisy-label methods.",
      "m-sharpness computed on small per-accelerator sub-batches correlates better with generalization."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
